<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Hoodoo to McKenzie Pass Traverse</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:259-2: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="44.405262" lon="-121.861126"><ele>1458.1</ele><name>Ray Benson Sno-park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:ray-benson-sno-park (OSM way 205969667); confidence: high; pdf_page: 261; quote: This 22-mile Backcountry tour from Ray Benson Sno-Park to the snow gate</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.371329" lon="-121.866298"><ele>1427.0</ele><name>Big Lake Youth Camp (east shore)</name><desc>source: OSM node 2159722866 Big Lake Youth Camp; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 262; quote: ski 2.5 miles to a road on the east shore of Big Lake ... then ski through the camp buildings along the shore</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.366681" lon="-121.858243"><ele>1468.9</ele><name>PCT south-east of the camp</name><desc>source: nearest OSM Pacific Crest Trail node (4285109660) to the camp's south side; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 262; quote: Ski out the south side and angle up to find the PCT, not always easy to locate</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.310893" lon="-121.819051"><ele>1616.9</ele><name>Leave the PCT east of the Washington-Belknap saddle</name><desc>source: OSM PCT node 12401597184, the PCT's low point (DEM 5,305) after the saddle; here the PCT turns up over Belknap's shoulder to 6,100 ft, above the book's 'stay below 5,600'; confidence: low; pdf_page: 262; quote: Climb to the 5,540-foot saddle between Belknap Crater and Mount Washington, then follow the contour around Belknap's east side, maintaining elevation then descending to McKenzie Pass</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.298000" lon="-121.812000"><ele>1630.5</ele><name>Contour east of Little Belknap 1</name><desc>source: placed on the DEM 5,300-5,400 ft band east of Little Belknap; confidence: low; pdf_page: 262; quote: Climb to the 5,540-foot saddle between Belknap Crater and Mount Washington, then follow the contour around Belknap's east side, maintaining elevation then descending to McKenzie Pass</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.288000" lon="-121.804000"><ele>1648.7</ele><name>Contour east of Little Belknap 2</name><desc>source: placed on the DEM 5,300-5,400 ft band east of Little Belknap; confidence: low; pdf_page: 262; quote: Climb to the 5,540-foot saddle between Belknap Crater and Mount Washington, then follow the contour around Belknap's east side, maintaining elevation then descending to McKenzie Pass</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.277000" lon="-121.804000"><ele>1646.4</ele><name>Contour east of Little Belknap 3</name><desc>source: placed on the DEM 5,300-5,400 ft band east of Little Belknap; confidence: low; pdf_page: 262; quote: Climb to the 5,540-foot saddle between Belknap Crater and Mount Washington, then follow the contour around Belknap's east side, maintaining elevation then descending to McKenzie Pass</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.268000" lon="-121.807000"><ele>1614.6</ele><name>Contour east of Little Belknap 4</name><desc>source: placed on the DEM 5,300-5,400 ft band east of Little Belknap; confidence: low; pdf_page: 262; quote: Climb to the 5,540-foot saddle between Belknap Crater and Mount Washington, then follow the contour around Belknap's east side, maintaining elevation then descending to McKenzie Pass</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.260200" lon="-121.800490"><ele>1622.8</ele><name>McKenzie Pass (Dee Wright Observatory)</name><desc>source: OSM saddle node 5373275217, as in or-vielbig-2e_258-1; confidence: high; pdf_page: 261; book_elev_ft: 5324; quote: map 59: McKENZIE PASS 5324'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.307631" lon="-121.705896"><ele>1227.5</ele><name>Highway 242 snow gate</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:hwy242-snow-gate = OSM node 38473692 (as in or-vielbig-2e_258-1); confidence: high; pdf_page: 262; book_elev_ft: 4040; quote: From the pass to the snow gate is 6.2 miles</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Hoodoo to McKenzie Pass Traverse</name><desc>1. Ray Benson Sno-park -&gt; Big Lake Youth Camp (east shore): osm (medium), 3.20 mi | 2. Big Lake Youth Camp (east shore) -&gt; PCT south-east of the camp: straight (low), 0.51 mi | 3. PCT south-east of the camp -&gt; Leave the PCT east of the Washington-Belknap saddle: osm (medium), 6.81 mi | 4. Leave the PCT east of the Washington-Belknap saddle -&gt; Contour east of Little Belknap 1: straight (low), 0.96 mi | 5. Contour east of Little Belknap 1 -&gt; Contour east of Little Belknap 2: straight (low), 0.80 mi | 6. Contour east of Little Belknap 2 -&gt; Contour east of Little Belknap 3: straight (low), 0.76 mi | 7. Contour east of Little Belknap 3 -&gt; Contour east of Little Belknap 4: straight (low), 0.64 mi | 8. Contour east of Little Belknap 4 -&gt; McKenzie Pass (Dee Wright Observatory): straight (low), 0.63 mi | 9. McKenzie Pass (Dee Wright Observatory) -&gt; Highway 242 snow gate: osm (high), 6.57 mi</desc>
